This program is a modified version of OrcaSlicer (https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer). OrcaSlicer is based on
Bambu Studio by Bambu Lab, which is based on PrusaSlicer by Prusa Research, which is based on Slic3r by Alessandro
Ranellucci and the RepRap community. It also carries work from SuperSlicer and from Ultimaker's CuraEngine (the
Arachne wall generator, AGPL-3.0-or-later).

engine/shims/tbb-serial is derived from the serial TBB shim of Hiosdra/OrcaWasm
(https://github.com/Hiosdra/OrcaWasm, AGPL-3.0).

Modified by Muon 3D Technologies Limited from September 2026: OrcaSlicer's libslic3r built headless for WebAssembly
(Emscripten); a bridge that runs OrcaSlicer's command-line slicing path without a GUI; a Web Worker host speaking
the protocol in packages/protocol; a settings catalogue generated from OrcaSlicer's option definitions and settings
tabs; and a TypeScript translation of OrcaSlicer's settings rules (ConfigManipulation.cpp, Tab.cpp). Changes to
OrcaSlicer's own files are the commits on branch muon3d-wasm of https://github.com/Muon-3D/OrcaSlicer after the
upstream base named in SOURCE.md, and the patches listed in engine/PATCHES.md.

